WEBVTT

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.440
Hey.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.900
Lunchtime is over.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.440
By the way, Tsubomaki-san,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.210
they've been holding the FSRS trials since yesterday, right?

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.980
Oh, is that so?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.110
What's this FSRS?

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:45.950
I can't believe you're in this business without knowing that.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.950
It's the abbreviation for Formula Stellar Racing School.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.920
Do you think it'll happen again?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:52.920
A total loss?

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.260
Yeah, it sure was a surprise last year.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.670
They ran out of school cars, so they went around asking,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:04.060
"Can we buy any of your spare Formula Stellar machines right away?"

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:09.950
They came around asking their rivals,
 so they must have wrecked a lot and run out.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.600
It's because they let softies drive.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.420
Those that drive with their parents' money without a real aim.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.560
They lack seriousness!

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.660
What of it?!  A total loss at the school?!

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.400
Now now, Komazawa.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.610
There's no need to get all worked up just because they dropped you at the application stage last year.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.090
They only pass those who have been driving since they were little.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.580
That's why they end up with slackers.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.040
Stop yapping.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.560
It's because they have those slackers driving for them

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:44.510
that we private teams have a chance against those teams with a manufacturer's support.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.360
We're counting on you.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.990
You're our ace after all.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.700
Defeat the FSRS!

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.020
Leave it to me!

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.760
<b>This is his first run today and he's already shortened his time by 0.6 seconds!</b>

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.720
Not bad, Shiba.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.350
This is the end of the free run.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.680
All cars pit in.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.290
Capeta...

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.360
What place is he in?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.540
Capeta...

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.920
I will now announce group A's best times in this session.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:35.360
Top time is Ishihara, 30.811 seconds!

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.930
He's shown pride as our regular driver.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.890
Clap clap clap clap!

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:43.010
Second is Shiba, 31 seconds flat!

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.520
All right, Shiba!

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.000
Keep this up and push your time down to the 30-second range!

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.800
Third: Hata, 31.37 seconds.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.990
Fourth: Daiki, 31.45 seconds.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.540
Fifth: Taira, 31.51 seconds.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.890
Sixth: Isa, 31.98 seconds.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.680
Everyone is within the 31-second range.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.350
That's quite impressive.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.300
But you should all be able to do better.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.760
Push it harder in the qualifier.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.010
We will now hold the free run session for group B,
 and then start the qualifiers straight after.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.790
Please be ready.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:22.690
Yes, sir!

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.640
So how was Capeta?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.920
He was in fifth place.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.610
Fifth place out of six!

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.050
Geez, what's he doing?!

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.100
I see.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.660
And how about Shiba-kun's rank?

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.380
Top time.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.620
Capeta's time is getting shorter, but...

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.540
Shiba is also coming along with a bang.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.320
That doesn't matter!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.760
What's the point of losing to a guy like that?!

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.440
Well, Shiba is quite a tough rival.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.630
Shut up!

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.670
Who are you supporting anyway?!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.830
Geez!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.140
Group A did pretty good this time.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.150
But, Kagami-san...

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:14.130
He said he'd pass two people like last year, right?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.610
But no matter how you look at it, we can only take one person this year.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.100
We have two regulars right now,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.610
and Naomi will be participating in the third machine starting in October, right?

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.330
We have drivers queued up.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:31.730
If we were to take one more,
Shiba stands out at the moment.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.840
Hata isn't too bad either.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.800
Yeah, she's got a record of 31.37 seconds.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.440
Um, can I say something?

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:44.190
Shiba's nearly reached the 30-second range, 

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.270
so your eyes are all on him, right?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:53.490
But there's someone who shortened his time by 1 second overnight.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.230
Look carefully.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.390
Taira... is it?

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.700
That's right.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:05.160
And his first time driving the FSte was the day before yesterday.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.660
Really on the spot.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.070
Are you serious?!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.390
Very serious.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:14.410
Of course you won't know until you see the final results, but...

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:18.670
Looking at the growth rate, he might go far.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.750
<b>Group B, free run finished!</b>

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.230
<b>We will start the qualifier for group A at 11 a.m.!</b>

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.370
<b>All cars hurry and set your new tires!</b>

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:37.480
All right.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.380
The first corner is going well as we discussed last night.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.470
You can do a bit more, so hang in there longer.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.170
Yes.

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:46.910
Second corner is good.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:50.660
The other place where you can shorten your time is on the last corner.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.630
You're stepping on the brake at the middle of the curve because you want to accelerate quickly, but...

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.530
Save the brake until you get closer to the exit of the curve and turn.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:06.880
Then the nose will turn into the corner deeply, and you can get into position to accelerate sooner.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.280
And then your speed on the main straight should be faster.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.230
Yes.

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:12.410
Okay, go!

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.900
You should at least be able to catch up to Shiba's time!

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:15.810
Okay!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.420
<b>We will now start the qualifier for group A.</b>

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:53.000
<b>All right, it's finally here!</b>

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.440
<b>The FSRS Grand Prix in Japan!</b>

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:01.690
In the grandstand, an audience of 35,000 hold their breath as they watch the time attack!

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.440
Makoto-san, you're getting overexcited...

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.380
Hey, Monami.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.690
Don't peek so much.  They'll get angry with you!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:13.250
What!  You're good at peeking yourself!

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:13.980
What?!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.710
Like I said, it wasn't me who was peeking during your bath!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.360
You're really persistent!

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:23.760
I-I'm sorry!

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.830
I'm really s—

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:31.580
See?

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.770
Go, Taira.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:44.820
Start your attack.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.620
<i>Deeper.  More!</i>

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:03.460
<i>At the second corner, wait until I'm in the right position!</i>

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.550
<i>Accel on!</i>

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:17.760
<i>Fourth corner, lightly brake.</i>

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.270
<i>Here it is, the fifth corner!</i>

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:23.740
<i>I can do it now!</i>

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:31.780
<i>The brake lamp didn't light up.</i>

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:35.460
<i>Did he only take his foot off the accel when he turned in?</i>

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:40.610
<i>Everyone else is using the brakes at that corner...</i>

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.710
<i>It's only our regular, Ishihara, who also doesn't brake.</i>

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.760
And I didn't even tell him.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.840
<i>Save the brakes until I get close to the end of the curve...</i>

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.840
<i>and accelerate!</i>

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:58.270
<b>Taira, 31.22 seconds!</b>

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.980
All right!

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.980
<b>It's here, it's here!</b>

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.290
<b>Taira also breaks his time!</b>

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.940
Hey, Shin-chan.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.130
Taira isn't bad, is he?

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:11.740
He's able to do whatever you tell him straight away.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.090
As well as even those things you haven't told him about...

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.960
Hey, Tanaka-san.  Did you notice?

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:21.580
His head is facing a different direction from the rest when he's driving.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:22.380
Look there!

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.380
The direction of his head?

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:29.080
He's now turning left, but his helmet is facing right, you see?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.300
Yeah.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.800
He's already looking ahead at the fourth corner.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.810
He's the only one who's looking far ahead.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.140
He might really go far.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.890
<b>Shiba is now at the final corner!</b>

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.070
<b>How is it?!</b>

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:54.530
It's out!  30.89 seconds!

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:56.760
Following Ishihara's time, 30.76 seconds,

00:11:56.760 --> 00:12:00.040
the first to reach the 30-second range out of all the students!

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.040
All right, Shiba!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.890
You're the only one who can drive the same line as Ishihara!

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.700
<i>Like I imagined!</i>

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.760
<b>Taira, 31.18 seconds!</b>

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:24.310
<b>He's shortened his time again!</b>

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.270
<i>Capeta...</i>

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:33.400
Well now, Taira-san, Capeta-kun isn't doing so bad either.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.860
O-Oh no.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.360
He's no match for Shiba-kun.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.250
He's now in the 30-second range, I hear?

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:46.530
Oh, well, Ryou had two days to practice.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.240
<i>Two days.</i>

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.180
<i>It's two days now since Capeta first drove this machine.</i>

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.280
<b>Shiba, 31 seconds flat!</b>

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.180
<b>Oh, so close!</b>

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.530
Ryou!

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:04.710
Calm down!

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.650
Remember when you practiced!

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.410
<i>Capeta...</i>

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.250
<i>You're too incredible.</i>

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:16.340
<i>Within two days, you caught up to someone who had practiced for two days.</i>

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:19.070
<i>You've succeeded completely.</i>

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:22.860
<i>I can't say this in front of Oka-san, but...</i>

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.250
<i>Capeta, you're way greater!</i>

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>This is...</i>

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.240
<i>This is so much fun!</i>

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:07.920
<i>Accel.</i>

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.120
<i>Brake.</i>

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.130
<i>Steer.</i>

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.200
<i>The machine moves the way I want it to.</i>

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.550
<i>There's no delay!</i>

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:20.160
<i>I have the feeling that I can bring my time down as much as I want!</i>

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.500
<i>I've never driven a machine like this!</i>

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.520
<i>This is so much fun!</i>

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:34.650
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:39.220
<i>This is the first time in his racing career...</i>

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.120
<i>that there's no handicap on the machine.</i>

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:44.870
<i>It was really irritating...</i>

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:51.880
<i>because I could only get him old karts and couldn't let him drive with his true abilities.</i>

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:56.460
<i>Give him an equal machine and this is what you get all of a sudden?!</i>

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.220
Go, Ca-chan!

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.020
Beat Shiba's time!

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.090
<b>Daiki, 31.28 seconds!</b>

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.650
<b>He's also shortening his time!</b>

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.600
The qualifying time attack!  Things are sure heating up!

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.580
Ishihara and then Shiba.  Following them is...

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.040
<b>Taira in third-place time!</b>

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.500
All right!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.500
Yay!!

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.330
<b>Oh, Ishihara!</b>

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:02.290
<b>He aggressively passes Isa, whose pace hasn't gotten better!</b>

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.100
Isa, can you hear me?

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.310
That was very dangerous when you got passed back there.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.880
Look at your mirrors carefully.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:24.500
Ishihara sure is getting hot.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.930
Moreover, the way Isa was passed was terrible.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:30.510
<b>Are Ishihara's true feelings coming out?!</b>

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.610
<b>That's right.</b>

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:35.060
<b>Last year he was unbelievably beaten by Minamoto, who was a student!</b>

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:38.650
<b>We teased him for a year after that.
  Those were sad days...</b>

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:43.110
<b>He seriously goes for the time attack as if to say, "It'll never happen again!"</b>

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.700
<i>Please... Someone stop Makoto-san...</i>

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.550
Listen, Isa.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:49.700
There's still plenty of time.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.610
<b>Your time is sure to get better as long as you don't rush yourself.</b>

00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:00.960
<i>For some of you, this may be your last day driving in the FSte today.</i>

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:03.920
<i>To be honest, the qualifier is everything.</i>

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.020
<i>My time...</i>

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.390
<i>I have to improve my time!</i>

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.260
<i>Capeta...</i>

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:27.560
<i>You were always being held back because of an old kart and I couldn't see it until now.</i>

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.690
<i>So this is how you've been driving, all this time.</i>

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.400
<i>Back then...</i>

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.820
<i>In exchange for us taking care of everything,</i>

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.380
<i>from the acquisition of your license to your participation in races,</i>

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:44.170
<i>we'll have you, Capeta-kun, become a part of our team, Autohouse Racing.</i>

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:45.760
<i>I don't want that!</i>

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:48.220
<i>I already have a team.</i>

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.180
<i>Right, Dad?</i>

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.410
<i>We're a team, right?</i>

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.810
<i>I... was too happy with Capeta's words...</i>

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.560
<i>and racing was such fun...</i>

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.360
<i>and we've come this far, but...</i>

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:06.630
<i>As a parent I should have... by force...</i>

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:08.840
<i>No, even after that!</i>

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.770
<i>Should I have put him in Autohouse?!</i>

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:12.490
<i>Then...</i>

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.490
<i>he wouldn't have had to push himself that hard!</i>

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:20.530
<i>If Capeta passes the audition...</i>

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:24.840
<i>Team Capeta will break up, but are you okay with that, Nobu-kun?</i>

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.330
<i>I asked him like that, but...</i>

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:32.430
<i>Honestly, the one who wanted to continue racing as Team Capeta...</i>

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.230
<i>was... me.</i>

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:03.960
<i>Okay!</i>

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.380
<i>I'll have this lap!</i>

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.380
<i>If I'm to beat Shiba, this is the lap!</i>

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.200
All right.  Good.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.660
This is the best so far!

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.350
He hasn't made any mistakes so far.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.310
He may be able to get a time in the 30-second range.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.860
<i>I'm going to be the one getting the scholarship!</i>

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:30.820
<i>My time...</i>

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.660
<i>I have to improve my time!</i>

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.320
<i>Just like I pictured it.</i>

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.370
<i>I don't use the brake at this corner.</i>

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:47.800
<i>I can't see the edge but I can make it!</i>

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.760
<i>I won't miss!</i>

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:52.720
<b>Isa spins on the fifth corner!</b>

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:54.220
What?!

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.680
<i>Accel off!</i>

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.140
<i>Turn in!</i>

00:19:58.930 --> 00:19:59.950
<i>I did it!</i>

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:01.100
<i>It's perfect!</i>

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:02.060
Oh no!

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:04.560
Taira, look out!  Dodge it!

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.300
<i>Don't hit!</i>

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:20.290
Taira, dodge it!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.310
Taira?!

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.160
<i>Is that Taira?!</i>

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.370
What was that noise?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.410
Huh, what?  What happened?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:12.550
I... don't know, but...

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:16.060
Is that... Capeta?

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:52.110
Why, Capeta?

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:57.080
You were doing so well, and then you crash?!

00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:00.360
You won't be able to pass if you break a machine!

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.260
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:02.200
Turning Point!

00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:04.210
Open up the future!
